  "result": {
    "summary": "Implementation matches the deterministic level() rules, the shadow/active harness depth machinery in daemon.py/spawn.py, the promotion.fast_path criteria (20-sample threshold, first-pass/token deltas, two-fix-round demotion, active self-refusal to shadow), and the decision_log additions. All listed acceptance test IDs are present as unittest.TestCase methods with `import _harness`, use tempfile/mock (no pytest fixtures), and the gate metadata shows 0 reds. Traced the fast-path pipeline stamping order in daemon.dispatch to confirm pipeline.harness_level/harness_mode are written before _dispatch_worker and spawn.run_worker read them via harness_depth.active(), so jev_route.shadow_context and spawn._prepare_skills are correctly skipped only for stamped level 0-1 tasks, while security-path review and hooks/tests-green remain untouched. Only note is a documented, not-explicitly-tested edge case around complexity==7 tasks landing at level 4 instead of the base spec's literal level 3 due to planner_taxonomy's existing complexity>=7 architectural heuristic; low severity since it's explicitly discussed in the docs and traceable to an authorized spec-review amendment (T-1094b).",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/harness_depth.py",
        "line": 44,
        "issue": "For complexity==7 tasks, planner_taxonomy.classify treats task_class=='architectural' (set because harness_depth.task_class already returns 'architectural' at complexity>=7) as architectural=True, so these tasks hit the level-4 'architectural' branch before the level-3 'complexity 6-7' elif is ever reached. The base spec's rule table says complexity 6-7 should be level 3; only complexity 6 actually lands there, complexity 7 always resolves to level 4. This is called out and rationalized in docs/hermes-hardening/15-harness-depth.md, and is consistent with spec review T-1094(b)'s 'whichever says architectural' language, but no acceptance test exercises complexity==7 directly, so the deviation from the literal table is unverified by the suite.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
